TestNG Annotation :
==================
  - Test


---------------------------
1)priority Attribute in Test anno -- it will only on the same class
  - this is parameter in @Test annotation and by default priority is "0"
  - It's run in alphabet order of the test method -if multiple methods are having same priority
  - It can have negative values order - -5 -4 -3 -3 -1 0 1 2 3 . this will execute lower to upper value
  - Priority can have random value (not seq) - test run as lower to higer
  - TestNG execute only the @test methods only

  Use "@Test(Priority=1/2/3)"
------------------------------
2)dependsOnMethods Attribte in Test anno -- it will be only the same class only
 -Depending on the specific test method(login) then excute the rest of the Method (search , logout)
 - Sinlge method , muliple methods can be mentioned (but all should execute )
 - Test method will be skipped if That dependent method is failed /skipped

 Use
   @Test(dependsOnMethods={"login"})
    void search()....